      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we first recognize that this sequence is an arithmetic series where the first term \\(a = 1\\), the common difference \\(d = 6\\), and the last term is 259. We need to find the number of terms in the series and then find the sum of the series.\n\n**Step 1: Find the number of terms.**\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence can be found using the formula:\n\\[\na_n = a + (n-1)d\n\\]\nFor the last term 259, we have:\n\\[\n259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n\\]\nSolving for \\(n\\):\n\\[\n259 = 1 + 6n - 6\n\\]\n\\[\n259 = 6n - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n264 = 6n\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 44\n\\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the series.\n\n**Step 2: Find the sum of the series.**\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series is given by:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n\\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Substituting the known values:\n\\[\nS_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Find the remainder when the sum is divided by 6.**\nWe need to find \\(5720 \\mod 6\\). First, we find the remainder of 5720 itself when divided by 6. We can do this by summing the remainders of the individual digits of 5720:\n\\[\n5 + 7 + 2 + 0 = 14\n\\]\nNext, we find the remainder of 14 when divided by 6:\n\\[\n14 \\div 6 = 2 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 2\n\\]\nSo, \\(5720 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{6}\\).\n\nThe remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
